{"name":"Chutney","hex":"#9f5e4e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chutney","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet or savory but usually spicy condiment, originally from eastern India, made from a variety of fruits and/or vegetables, often containing significant amounts of fresh green or dried red chili peppers. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A style of Indo-Caribbean music from the West Indies, associated especially with Trinidad and Tobago."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chutney"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chutney","blocks":[{"text":"A chutney is a condiment associated with cuisines of the Indian subcontinent. Chutneys are made in a wide variety of forms, some raw such as with coriander, others cooked with sugar, like mango chutney. During the British Raj, Anglo-Indian cuisine adapted Indian chutney and brought it back to Britain, where green mango chutney in particular became popular. In the Western world, chutneys may be made with local fruits and vegetables, or purchased."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Chutneykarnataka.jpg/330px-Chutneykarnataka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chutney"},{"title":"Chutney (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Chutney is a 2016 Indian short film written by Jyoti Kapur Das, Tisca Chopra and Avneesh Mishra and directed by Jyoti Kapur Das. The story is situated at Model Town where Vanita played by Tisca Chopra is shown narrating a tale to a woman who, the night before, flirts with her husband at a party. The story is sweet, and spicy, just like Chutney. It is produced by Tisca Chopra; starring Adil Hussain, Tisca Chopra and Rasika Dugal. Additional cast- Sumit Gulati, Devesh Ranjan and Aakash Bharadwaj."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chutney_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Chutney_being_hand-mad